<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-J.Boag abnormals boost yr net profit.</title>
<headline>RTRS-J.Boag abnormals boost yr net profit.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 26</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     0.23 vs 1.27</p>
<p>    Net			    profit 32.11 vs loss 32.94</p>
<p>    Sales				   83.73 vs 178.49</p>
<p>    Other income			   3.24 vs 37.98</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		   profit 0.93 vs loss</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	     profit 29.23 vs loss 34.16</p>
<p>    Tax			    benefit 2.64 vs expense 0.04</p>
<p>    Interest				 9.32 vs 17.71</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   2.53 vs 3.75</p>
<p>NOTE: J.Boag and Son Ltd is a Tasmanian-based brewer. The company said the abnormal profit was associated with the company's refinancing.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
